.*********************************************************************
.*                                                                   *
.*  XAIO  -  STANDALONE CHANNEL I/O FOR ESA/390                      *
.*                                                                   *
.*  DMKCKP, DMKDMP, DMKLD00E AND DMKSAV DRIVE THE CHANNEL THEMSELVES *
.*  RATHER THAN THROUGH DMKIOS, BECAUSE THEY RUN BEFORE THE          *
.*  SCHEDULER EXISTS OR AFTER IT HAS STOPPED.  BETWEEN THEM THEY     *
.*  HOLD SEVENTY-SEVEN OF CP'S ONE HUNDRED AND THIRTY-THREE CHANNEL  *
.*  SITES, ALL IN ONE IDIOM:                                         *
.*                                                                   *
.*           ST    RX,CAW         SET THE CCW ADDRESS                *
.*           TIO   0(R2)          DRAIN -- IS IT FREE                *
.*           BNZ   *-4                                               *
.*           SIO   0(R2)          START                              *
.*           TIO   0(R2)          POLL FOR COMPLETION                *
.*           BC    6,*-4                                             *
.*           CLC   CSW+4(2),=AL1(CE+DE,0)                            *
.*                                                                   *
.*  CONVERTING SEVENTY-SEVEN SITES BY HAND IS SEVENTY-SEVEN CHANCES  *
.*  TO GET A CONDITION CODE BACKWARDS, WHICH IS WHAT RISKS R-01 AND  *
.*  R-02 ARE ABOUT.  SO THE REASONING HAPPENS ONCE, HERE.            *
.*                                                                   *
.*  THE IDEA THAT MAKES THIS CHEAP:  XATIO REBUILDS A CSW AT THE     *
.*  ARCHITECTED CSW LOCATION FROM THE IRB.  EVERY EXISTING           *
.*  CLC CSW+4(2) AND MVC SAVECSW(12),CSW THEREFORE KEEPS WORKING     *
.*  UNCHANGED, SO ONLY THE INSTRUCTIONS NEED CONVERTING AND NOT THE  *
.*  STATUS LOGIC, WHICH IS THE BULK OF THE CODE.  THE SAME SHIM IS   *
.*  ALREADY PROVEN IN DMKIOS -- IOSXCC1 IN XA0004DK.                 *
.*                                                                   *
.*  CONDITION CODES ARE NORMALISED TO WHAT S/370 WOULD HAVE SET, SO  *
.*  THE BRANCHES AROUND EACH SITE ARE LEFT ALONE:                    *
.*                                                                   *
.*      SIO  CC0 STARTED   CC1 CSW STORED  CC2 BUSY  CC3 NOT OPER    *
.*      SSCH CC0 STARTED   CC1 STATUS PEND CC2 BUSY  CC3 NOT OPER    *
.*        -- CC0, CC2 AND CC3 ALREADY AGREE.  CC1 DIFFERS IN         *
.*           WORDING ONLY: BOTH MEAN "GO LOOK AT THE STATUS".        *
.*                                                                   *
.*      TIO  CC0 AVAILABLE CC1 CSW STORED  CC2 BUSY  CC3 NOT OPER    *
.*      TSCH CC0 IRB STORED (STATUS WAS PENDING)                     *
.*           CC1 NO STATUS PENDING         CC3 NOT OPER              *
.*        -- CC0 AND CC1 ARE **INVERTED**.  TIO CC0 MEANS THE DEVICE *
.*           IS FREE; TSCH CC1 MEANS NOTHING IS PENDING, WHICH IS    *
.*           THE SAME FACT.  XATIO SWAPS THEM BACK.  THIS IS THE     *
.*           SINGLE MOST LIKELY THING TO GET WRONG IN THE WHOLE      *
.*           CONVERSION, AND IT IS NOW WRITTEN IN ONE PLACE.         *
.*                                                                   *
.*  ALL THREE MACROS PRESERVE EVERY CALLER REGISTER.  THE WORK AREA  *
.*  IS NOT REENTRANT, WHICH SUITS STANDALONE CODE AND SUITS NOTHING  *
.*  ELSE -- DO NOT USE THESE IN DMKIOS.                              *
.*                                                                   *
.*  EACH MACRO EXPANDS TO FOUR INSTRUCTIONS AND CALLS A SUBROUTINE    *
.*  THAT XAIOWORK EMITS ONCE.  THE FIRST DRAFT EXPANDED THE WHOLE     *
.*  BODY INLINE, ABOUT FIFTEEN INSTRUCTIONS, AND DMKDMP THEN FAILED   *
.*  WITH  IFO209 ADDRESSABILITY ERROR  ON TWO OF ITS OWN PRE-EXISTING *
.*  LINES:  TWENTY-TWO SITES AT SIXTY BYTES APIECE PUSHED THE MODULE  *
.*  PAST THE 8 KB ITS TWO BASE REGISTERS COVER, AND THE LITERAL POOL  *
.*  FELL OUT OF REACH.  THESE MODULES ARE ALREADY NEAR THEIR LIMIT,   *
.*  SO CALL-SITE SIZE IS A HARD CONSTRAINT, NOT A PREFERENCE.  I-56.  *
.*                                                                   *
.*  THE MODULE MUST INVOKE  XAIOWORK  ONCE IN ITS OWN CSECT.         *
.*                                                                   *
.*********************************************************************
         MACRO
&NAME    XAIOWORK &CAW=CAW,&CSW=CSW
.*  WORK AREAS AND THE DEVICE-TO-SUBCHANNEL SUBROUTINE.  ONE PER
.*  MODULE, ANYWHERE IN ITS CSECT.
&NAME    DS    0H
XAIOSAVE DS    4F             CALLER'S R14, R15, R0, R1
XAIOSB   DS    1F             THE SUBROUTINES' OWN LINKAGE
XAIOORB  DS    8F             THE ORB -- THIRTY-TWO BYTES
XAIOIRB  DS    16F            THE IRB -- SIXTY-FOUR BYTES
XAIOSCHB DS    13F            THE SCHIB -- FIFTY-TWO, FULLWORD ALIGNED
XAIOSSID DS    1F             SUBSYSTEM ID OF THE DEVICE WE LAST FOUND
XAIODEV  DS    1H             THE DEVICE ADDRESS THAT SSID BELONGS TO
         DS    1H             ALIGNMENT
XAIOPFX  DC    X'00010000'    SUBSYSTEM ID PREFIX, LOGICAL CHANNEL SS 0
XAIONSCH DC    AL2(256)       SUBCHANNELS SEARCHED
XAIOFF   DC    X'FF'          ALL ONES -- THE ONLY WAY TO SET CC3
XAIO00   DC    X'00'          ALL ZEROS.  WITH XAIOFF THESE TWO SET
.*  EVERY CONDITION CODE WITHOUT A REGISTER, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT:
.*      TM  XAIO00,X'FF'   ALL ZERO      -> CC0
.*      CLI XAIO00,X'01'   OPERAND LOW   -> CC1
.*      CLI XAIOFF,X'01'   OPERAND HIGH  -> CC2
.*      TM  XAIOFF,X'FF'   ALL ONES      -> CC3
.*  AN EARLIER DRAFT RETURNED THE CODE IN R15 AND SET THE CC WITH LTR
.*  OR LCR.  THAT IS WRONG IN ANY MODULE WHOSE USING BASE IS R15 --
.*  FIFTY-FOUR OF CP'S 201, INCLUDING ELEVEN THIS CONVERSION TOUCHES --
.*  BECAUSE EVERY REFERENCE IN THIS WORK AREA RESOLVES THROUGH THAT
.*  SAME BASE.  DMKOPR IS  USING DMKOPRWT,R15 , SO THE FIRST SR R15,R15
.*  DESTROYED THE BASE AND THE NEXT SUBCHANNEL INSTRUCTION TOOK AN
.*  OPERAND EXCEPTION ON A SUBSYSTEM ID READ OUT OF LOW STORAGE.  NO
.*  REGISTER IS SAFE TO BORROW: EVERY ONE OF THE SIXTEEN IS A USING
.*  BASE SOMEWHERE IN CP, AND R0 IS RESERVED BECAUSE EVERY CALLER HAS
.*  USING PSA,R0 .  SO BORROW NONE.  I-106.
XAIOMODE DC    X'00'          0 UNKNOWN, 1 = S/370, 2 = ESA/390
         DS    0F             ALIGNMENT
XAIOSB2  DS    1F             R14 ACROSS THE ARCHITECTURE PROBE
XAIOSB3  DS    1F             R1 ACROSS IT TOO -- SEE XAIOPROB
XAIOPSAV DS    1D             THE CALLER'S PROGRAM NEW PSW, SAVED
.*  THE DS 0D IS LOAD-BEARING.  A BARE HEX DC DOES NOT ALIGN, BUT THE
.*  A-TYPE AFTER IT DOES -- SO WITHOUT THIS THE ASSEMBLER PADS BETWEEN
.*  THEM AND THE EIGHT BYTES THE MVC COPIES ARE NOT THE PSW.  THAT IS
.*  THE IFO220 ALIGNMENT ERROR THE FIRST DRAFT EARNED.  I-97.
         DS    0D             SO THE PAIR IS ALIGNED AND CONTIGUOUS
XAIOPPSW DC    X'000C0000'    EC MODE, AND VALID IN BOTH S/370 AND
         DC    A(XAIOPS37)    ESA/390 -- THE PROBE'S RECOVERY PSW
.*
.*  XAIOPROB -- WHICH MACHINE IS THIS ?  CALLED BAL R14, ONCE.
.*
.*  DMKSAV RUNS ON BOTH PATHS AND CANNOT BE COMPILED FOR EITHER: THE
.*  NUCLEUS BUILD EXECUTES IT ON A S/370 MACHINE -- THAT IS WHAT
.*  WRITES SYSRES -- AND THE DISK IPL REACHES IT THROUGH DMKCKP'S
.*  GOTO DMKSAVRS ON AN ESA/390 ONE.  I-96.  REVERTING IT BROKE THE
.*  SECOND; CONVERTING IT BREAKS THE FIRST.  SO ASK THE MACHINE.
.*
.*  THIS IS CP'S OWN IDIOM: DMKCPI DETECTS THE ECPS:VM ASSISTS BY
.*  EXECUTING ONE AND RECOVERING FROM THE PROGRAM CHECK.  STSCH IS
.*  THE PROBE HERE BECAUSE IT EXISTS ONLY IN ESA/390, TAKES AN
.*  OPERATION EXCEPTION IN S/370, AND CHANGES NOTHING WHEN IT WORKS.
.*
.*  EVERY CALLER HAS  USING PSA,R0  IN FORCE, SO PRNPSW RESOLVES.
.*  THE PROGRAM INTERRUPTION DOES NOT DISTURB THE GENERAL REGISTERS,
.*  SO R14 SURVIVES THE TRAP AND THE RETURN IS THE SAME EITHER WAY.
XAIOPROB DS    0H
.*  R1 IS THE CALLER'S DEVICE NUMBER AND THE PROBE NEEDS R1 FOR ITS
.*  OWN SUBSYSTEM ID, SO IT MUST HAND THE DEVICE BACK.  IT DID NOT,
.*  AND THE CONSEQUENCE WAS INVISIBLE FOR WEEKS BECAUSE THE PROBE RUNS
.*  EXACTLY ONCE PER MODULE: WHICHEVER DEVICE HAPPENED TO BE THE FIRST
.*  XAIO CALL HAD ITS NUMBER REPLACED BY X'00010000' AND WAS THEN
.*  LOOKED UP AS DEVICE X'0000', WHICH NO PMCW MATCHES, SO XAIOFIND
.*  RETURNED CC3 -- NOT OPERATIONAL -- FOR A DEVICE THAT WAS PRESENT
.*  AND HEALTHY.  IN DMKCPI THAT DEVICE WAS 6A1, THE IPL DEVICE AND
.*  SYSRES, SO CP READ A VOLUME LABEL FROM EVERY PACK EXCEPT THE ONE
.*  IT WAS ABOUT TO GO LOOKING FOR, AND ENDED AT ABEND CPI001.
.*  ONE VICTIM, CHOSEN BY CALL ORDER, IS WHY THIS LOOKED LIKE A
.*  PROPERTY OF THE IPL DEVICE RATHER THAN A CLOBBERED REGISTER.
.*  I-108.
         ST    R1,XAIOSB3     KEEP THE CALLER'S DEVICE
         MVC   XAIOPSAV(8),PRNPSW   BORROW THE CALLER'S HANDLER
         MVC   PRNPSW(8),XAIOPPSW   AND POINT IT AT OUR RECOVERY
         MVI   XAIOMODE,X'02'       ASSUME ESA/390
         L     R1,XAIOPFX     SUBCHANNEL ZERO, WHICH ALWAYS ANSWERS
         STSCH XAIOSCHB       ESA/390 ONLY.  A S/370 TRAPS HERE.
XAIOPBAK DS    0H             BOTH OUTCOMES REJOIN HERE
         MVC   PRNPSW(8),XAIOPSAV   GIVE THE HANDLER BACK
         L     R1,XAIOSB3     AND THE DEVICE, UNTOUCHED
         BR    R14
XAIOPS37 DS    0H             THE STSCH TRAPPED: THIS IS A S/370
         MVI   XAIOMODE,X'01'
         B     XAIOPBAK
.*
.*  EACH ENTRY POINT PROBES ONCE, THEN TAKES THE NATIVE PATH.  IN
.*  S/370 THE ORIGINAL INSTRUCTION IS SIMPLY ISSUED: R1 ALREADY HOLDS
.*  THE DEVICE ADDRESS, THE HARDWARE STORES THE CSW AT X'40' ITSELF,
.*  AND THE CONDITION CODES ARE THE ONES THE CALLER WAS WRITTEN FOR,
.*  SO NOTHING NEEDS TRANSLATING.
.*
.*  XAIOFIND -- DEVICE ADDRESS IN R1, SUBSYSTEM ID RETURNED IN R1,
.*  CONDITION CODE 3 AND R1 ZERO IF THERE IS NO SUCH DEVICE.
.*  CALLED BALR R14.  USES R0, R1, R14, R15 ONLY.
.*
.*  THIS SCANS THE SUBCHANNELS WITH STSCH RATHER THAN CONSULTING
.*  RDEVSSID, DELIBERATELY.  DMKDMP RUNS AFTER AN ABEND, WHEN CP'S
.*  CONTROL BLOCKS ARE EXACTLY WHAT CANNOT BE TRUSTED, AND A DUMP
.*  THAT NEEDS A HEALTHY RDEVBLOK TO WRITE ITSELF IS NO USE.  THE
.*  COST IS UP TO 256 STSCHS PER LOOKUP, PAID A HANDFUL OF TIMES IN
.*  CODE THAT RUNS ONCE.
.*
XAIOFIND DS    0H
.*  R0 IS NEVER TOUCHED HERE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.  EVERY CALLER SO
.*  FAR HAS  USING PSA,R0  IN FORCE, SO R0 MUST STAY ZERO FOR CAW AND
.*  CSW TO RESOLVE -- AND THE MACROS REFERENCE BOTH *BEFORE* THEY
.*  RESTORE REGISTERS.  AN EARLIER DRAFT USED R0 AS THE SUBCHANNEL
.*  COUNTER AND WOULD HAVE LEFT IT NON-ZERO ON RETURN, SILENTLY
.*  DISPLACING EVERY LOWCORE REFERENCE IN THE EXPANSION BY THE
.*  SUBCHANNEL NUMBER.  R15 IS THE COUNTER INSTEAD, AND THE DEVICE
.*  NUMBER IS MATCHED WITH CLC SO NO REGISTER IS NEEDED FOR IT.
         CH    R1,XAIODEV     SAME DEVICE AS LAST TIME ?
         BNE   XAIOSRCH       NO, GO AND LOOK
         L     R1,XAIOSSID    YES, REUSE THE ANSWER
         LTR   R1,R1          DID WE FIND ONE LAST TIME ?
         BZ    XAIONONE       NO -- CACHED "NO SUCH DEVICE"
         BR    R14            FOUND.  ANY CC BUT 3 WILL DO
XAIOSRCH DS    0H
         STH   R1,XAIODEV     REMEMBER WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR
         XC    XAIOSSID,XAIOSSID  NOTHING FOUND YET
         L     R1,XAIOPFX     X'00010000' -- SUBCHANNEL ZERO
.*  R1 IS THE COUNTER AS WELL AS THE OPERAND.  THE SUBSYSTEM ID IS THE
.*  PREFIX IN THE HIGH HALFWORD AND THE SUBCHANNEL NUMBER IN THE LOW,
.*  SO INCREMENTING IT *IS* STEPPING TO THE NEXT SUBCHANNEL, AND THE
.*  SEPARATE COUNTER R15 USED TO BE IS NOT NEEDED AT ALL.  THE DEVICE
.*  NUMBER WAS STASHED IN XAIODEV ABOVE, SO NOTHING ELSE WANTS R1.
XAIOLOOP DS    0H
         STSCH XAIOSCHB       STORE SUBCHANNEL
         BC    7,XAIONEXT     NOT CC0: NOT PROVIDED, TRY THE NEXT
         TM    XAIOSCHB+5,X'01' IS THE SUBCHANNEL VALID ?
         BZ    XAIONEXT       NO DEVICE BEHIND IT
         CLC   XAIODEV,XAIOSCHB+6 DOES THE PMCW DEVICE NUMBER MATCH ?
         BE    XAIOGOT        YES
XAIONEXT DS    0H
         LA    R1,1(0,R1)     NEXT SUBCHANNEL, IN THE ID ITSELF
         CLM   R1,B'0011',XAIONSCH  SEARCHED THEM ALL ?
         BL    XAIOLOOP       NO, KEEP GOING
XAIONONE DS    0H
         SR    R1,R1          NOT FOUND -- RETURN ZERO
         TM    XAIOFF,X'FF'   AND SET CONDITION CODE 3.  NOTHING IN
*                             THE LTR FAMILY CAN SET CC3 AT ALL.
         BR    R14
XAIOGOT  DS    0H
         ST    R1,XAIOSSID    REMEMBER IT FOR NEXT TIME
.*  ENABLE THE SUBCHANNEL BEFORE ANYONE TRIES TO USE IT.  SA22-7201-08
.*  ON THE PMCW'S E BIT: "WHEN THE E BIT IS ZERO ... I/O INSTRUCTIONS
.*  OTHER THAN MODIFY SUBCHANNEL AND STORE SUBCHANNEL THAT ARE EXECUTED
.*  FOR THE DESIGNATED SUBCHANNEL CAUSE CONDITION CODE 3 TO BE SET ...
.*  INITIALLY, ALL SUBCHANNELS ARE NOT ENABLED; IPL CAUSES THE IPL I/O
.*  DEVICE TO BECOME ENABLED."
.*
.*  THAT IS WHY THE SCAN ABOVE SUCCEEDS WHILE EVERY SSCH FAILS: STSCH
.*  IS EXEMPT, SO DEVICE NUMBERS RESOLVE CORRECTLY AND THEN NOTHING
.*  CAN BE STARTED.  ONLY THE IPL DEVICE WORKED -- WHICH IS EXACTLY
.*  WHY DMKSAV COULD READ THE WHOLE NUCLEUS OFF 6A1 AND DMKCPI COULD
.*  NOT BRING A SINGLE OTHER DEVICE ONLINE.  I-87.
.*
.*  E IS BIT 8 OF PMCW WORD 1 -- X'80' OF THE SAME BYTE WHOSE X'01'
.*  THE VALID TEST ABOVE ALREADY READS.  THE SEQUENCE IS THE ONE
.*  PROVEN BY EXECUTION IN tests/hardware/05-channel-subsystem.rc:
.*  STSCH, OI SCHIB+5 X'80', MSCH.  MSCH TAKES THE SSID IN R1, WHICH
.*  IS STILL THERE, AND THE SCHIB THE SCAN JUST STORED.
         TM    XAIOSCHB+5,X'80'  ENABLED ALREADY ?
         BO    XAIOGOTE       YES -- THE IPL DEVICE IS
         OI    XAIOSCHB+5,X'80'  ENABLE IT
         MSCH  XAIOSCHB       AND HAND THE SCHIB BACK
.*  MSCH'S OWN CONDITION CODE IS DELIBERATELY NOT TESTED.  IF IT
.*  REFUSES, THE CALLER'S SSCH STILL ANSWERS CC3 AND THE CALLER
.*  ALREADY HANDLES THAT -- SO CHECKING HERE WOULD ADD A SECOND PLACE
.*  TO GET THE SAME ANSWER WRONG.
XAIOGOTE DS    0H
         CLI   XAIOFF,X'01'   OPERAND HIGH, SO CC2 -- ANYTHING BUT CC3,
*                             WHICH IS ALL THE CALLERS TEST
         BR    R14
.*
.*  THE THREE SUBROUTINES.  ENTERED WITH THE DEVICE ADDRESS IN R1 AND
.*  THE RETURN ADDRESS IN R14.  THEY SET THE CONDITION CODE AND RETURN
.*  IT THROUGH BR R14, WHICH DOES NOT ALTER IT.  THE CALL-SITE MACRO
.*  HAS ALREADY SAVED AND WILL RESTORE R14, R15, R0 AND R1.
.*
XAIOSIO  DS    0H             START AN I/O
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'00' DO WE KNOW WHICH MACHINE YET ?
         BNE   XAIOSIOA       YES
         ST    R14,XAIOSB2    NO -- ASK, KEEPING THE RETURN
         BAL   R14,XAIOPROB
         L     R14,XAIOSB2
XAIOSIOA DS    0H
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'01' A S/370 ?
         BNE   XAIOSIOE       NO -- THE SUBCHANNEL PATH BELOW
         SIO   0(R1)          S/370: R1 IS ALREADY THE DEVICE
         BR    R14            AND THE CC IS ALREADY RIGHT
XAIOSIOE DS    0H             ESA/390 FROM HERE
         ST    R14,XAIOSB     OUR OWN RETURN, NOT THE CALLER'S SAVE
         XC    XAIOORB(12),XAIOORB  CLEAR THE ARCHITECTED TWELVE
.*  THE INTERRUPTION PARAMETER IS THE DEVICE ADDRESS, AS DMKCPI'S MSCH
.*  SETS IT (I-47): DMKDMP TELLS ITS DUMP DEVICE'S INTERRUPT BY IT,
.*  AND A ZERO HERE LEFT THE DUMP WAITING FOREVER (I-201).
         STH   R1,XAIOORB+2   INTERRUPTION PARAMETER = DEVICE
         BAL   R14,XAIOFIND   FIND THE SUBCHANNEL
         L     R14,XAIOSB
         BC    1,XAIOSIOX     CC3 -- NOT OPERATIONAL, PASS IT ON
.*  FLAG5 COMES FROM ORBCCWFM IN XABLOKS, WHICH IS THE ONE PLACE THE
.*  CCW FORMAT IS CHOSEN.  ZERO MEANS FORMAT 0 -- THE S/370 LAYOUT --
.*  SO EVERY EXISTING CHANNEL PROGRAM WORKS UNCONVERTED.  R-27.
         MVI   XAIOORB+5,ORBCCWFM CCW FORMAT
         MVI   XAIOORB+6,X'80' LOGICAL PATH MASK -- NOT ZERO
         MVC   XAIOORB+8(4),&CAW CCW ADDRESS THE CALLER SET
         SSCH  XAIOORB        START SUBCHANNEL
XAIOSIOX DS    0H             CC IS ALREADY SIO-COMPATIBLE
         BR    R14
.*
XAIOTIO  DS    0H             TEST AN I/O
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'00' DO WE KNOW WHICH MACHINE YET ?
         BNE   XAIOTIOA       YES
         ST    R14,XAIOSB2    NO -- ASK, KEEPING THE RETURN
         BAL   R14,XAIOPROB
         L     R14,XAIOSB2
XAIOTIOA DS    0H
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'01' A S/370 ?
         BNE   XAIOTIOE       NO -- THE SUBCHANNEL PATH BELOW
         TIO   0(R1)          S/370: HARDWARE STORES THE CSW
         BR    R14
XAIOTIOE DS    0H             ESA/390 FROM HERE
         ST    R14,XAIOSB
         BAL   R14,XAIOFIND
         L     R14,XAIOSB
         BC    1,XAIOTIOX     CC3 -- NOT OPERATIONAL, PASS IT ON
         TSCH  XAIOIRB        TEST SUBCHANNEL
         BC    4,XAIOTIOF     CC1: NOTHING PENDING -- BUT SEE BELOW
         BC    3,XAIOTIOX     CC2 OR CC3: PASS THEM ON UNCHANGED
.*  CC0 FROM TSCH: STATUS WAS PENDING, SO THE IRB HOLDS IT.  BUILD THE
.*  CSW THE CALLER'S CODE EXPECTS.  IRB+8 IS UNIT STATUS, +9 CHANNEL
.*  STATUS, +10 THE RESIDUAL COUNT, AND +4 THE CCW ADDRESS.
         MVI   &CSW,X'00'     KEY, ZEROES, CCW ADDRESS HIGH BYTE
         MVC   &CSW+1(3),XAIOIRB+5 CCW ADDRESS
         MVC   &CSW+4(4),XAIOIRB+8 UNIT AND CHANNEL STATUS, COUNT
         CLI   XAIO00,X'01'   TELL THE CALLER "CSW STORED", WHICH IS
*                             CC1: OPERAND X'00' IS LOW AGAINST X'01'.
         BR    R14
.*  TSCH CC1 IS "IRB STORED, SUBCHANNEL NOT STATUS-PENDING".  THE FIRST
.*  DRAFT READ THAT AS S/370 TIO CC0, DEVICE AVAILABLE, WHICH IS THE
.*  LITERAL EQUIVALENT AND THE WRONG ANSWER.  CP POLLS LIKE THIS:
.*
.*      TIO  0(R2)         TEST IO
.*      BC   6,*-4         LOOP IF BUSY OR STATUS STORED
.*
.*  -- IT LOOPS ON CC1 AND CC2 AND LEAVES ON CC0, DRAINING STATUS UNTIL
.*  THE DEVICE IS IDLE, AND THEN READS THE CSW OF THE LAST STATUS.  IN
.*  S/370 A DEVICE WITH AN OPERATION IN FLIGHT ANSWERS TIO WITH CC2,
.*  BUSY.  IN ESA/390 THAT SAME SUBCHANNEL IS SIMPLY NOT STATUS-PENDING
.*  AND TSCH ANSWERS CC1.  MAPPING IT TO CC0 LET THE LOOP OUT ON THE
.*  FIRST POLL, BEFORE THE I/O HAD FINISHED, AND CP THEN TESTED A CSW
.*  THAT HAD NEVER BEEN BUILT.  THE SCSW SAYS WHICH IT IS: FUNCTION
.*  CONTROL AND ACTIVITY CONTROL ARE NON-ZERO WHILE A FUNCTION IS IN
.*  PROGRESS.  I-93.
XAIOTIOF DS    0H             CC1: NO STATUS -- IDLE OR STILL RUNNING ?
         TM    XAIOIRB+2,X'7F' FUNCTION OR ACTIVITY CONTROL SET ?
         BNZ   XAIOTIOB       YES -- S/370 WOULD HAVE SAID BUSY
         TM    XAIOIRB+3,X'E0' SUBCHANNEL, DEVICE OR SUSPENDED ?
         BNZ   XAIOTIOB       YES -- BUSY
         TM    XAIO00,X'FF'   TRULY IDLE: ALL ZERO, SO CC0
         BR    R14
XAIOTIOB DS    0H             BUSY.  CC2.
         CLI   XAIOFF,X'01'   OPERAND X'FF' IS HIGH AGAINST X'01',
*                             WHICH IS CC2 WHERE XAIO00 GAVE CC1
XAIOTIOX DS    0H
         BR    R14
.*
XAIOHIO  DS    0H             HALT.  HSCH REPLACES BOTH HIO AND HDV:
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'00' DO WE KNOW WHICH MACHINE YET ?
         BNE   XAIOHIOA       YES
         ST    R14,XAIOSB2    NO -- ASK, KEEPING THE RETURN
         BAL   R14,XAIOPROB
         L     R14,XAIOSB2
XAIOHIOA DS    0H
         CLI   XAIOMODE,X'01' A S/370 ?
         BNE   XAIOHIOE       NO -- THE SUBCHANNEL PATH BELOW
         HIO   0(R1)          S/370
         BR    R14
XAIOHIOE DS    0H             ESA/390 FROM HERE
.*  THE DISTINCTION WAS BETWEEN HALTING A CHANNEL AND HALTING A
.*  DEVICE, AND A SUBCHANNEL IS ALWAYS ONE DEVICE.
         ST    R14,XAIOSB
         BAL   R14,XAIOFIND
         L     R14,XAIOSB
         BC    1,XAIOHIOX     CC3 -- NOT OPERATIONAL, PASS IT ON
         HSCH  0              HALT SUBCHANNEL
XAIOHIOX DS    0H
         BR    R14
.*  A MACRO THAT EMITS STORAGE MUST HAND BACK THE ALIGNMENT IT WAS
.*  GIVEN.  WITHOUT THIS, XAIOWORK'S LENGTH DECIDES THE ALIGNMENT OF
.*  WHATEVER THE MODULE DECLARES NEXT -- AND DMKCKP DECLARES WAIT17,
.*  WHICH  LPSW WAIT17  AT 00349100 REQUIRES TO BE DOUBLEWORD ALIGNED.
.*  ADDING THE ARCHITECTURE PROBE CHANGED THE LENGTH BY AN ODD NUMBER
.*  OF WORDS AND EARNED IFO220 IN A STATEMENT THIS CONVERSION NEVER
.*  TOUCHED, SEVERAL HUNDRED LINES AWAY.  I-97.
         DS    0D             LEAVE THE LOCATION COUNTER AS FOUND
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XASIO  &DEV
.*  &DEV IS THE REGISTER HOLDING THE DEVICE ADDRESS -- EXACTLY WHAT
.*  SIO 0(&DEV) TOOK.  THE CCW ADDRESS COMES FROM THE CAW, WHICH THE
.*  S/370 CODE ALWAYS SET FIRST AND WHICH IS NOW AN ORDINARY WORD OF
.*  CP'S STORAGE, SO THAT STORE IS LEFT IN PLACE.
.*  STM R14,R1 STORES R14, R15, R0 AND R1 BY WRAPPING, AND LM RESTORES
.*  THEM WITHOUT DISTURBING THE CONDITION CODE THE SUBROUTINE SET.
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         LR    R1,&DEV
         BAL   R14,XAIOSIO
         LM    R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XATIO  &DEV
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         LR    R1,&DEV
         BAL   R14,XAIOTIO
         LM    R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XAHIO  &DEV
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         LR    R1,&DEV
         BAL   R14,XAIOHIO
         LM    R14,R1,XAIOSAVE
         MEND
